Keep module-map flags out of ThinLTO backend compiles.

`compile_actions` includes `lto_backend`, so `module_map_home_cwd` adds
`-Xclang -fmodule-map-file-home-is-cwd` to every CcLtoBackendCompile action.
That flag is meaningless for an `-x ir` compile, but it makes the command
line of a "shared non-LTO backend" action depend on whether the rule that
created it had `module_maps` enabled. Bazel dedups those shareable actions
only when their command lines are identical, so a cc_library/cc_shared_library
(module_maps on) and a rules_rust rust_library (module_maps hardcoded off)
registering a backend for the same bitcode object produce an
"is generated by these conflicting actions" analysis failure under
--features=thin_lto (e.g. @rosdistro//cc:zenoh-cpp vs @zenoh-c//:zenohc_static
with --config=portable). Scope the args to `source_compile_actions`, which is
`compile_actions` minus `lto_backend`.

--- a/toolchain/features/BUILD.bazel
+++ b/toolchain/features/BUILD.bazel
@@ -646,7 +646,7 @@
 cc_args(
     name = "module_map_home_cwd_args",
     actions = [
-        "@rules_cc//cc/toolchains/actions:compile_actions",
+        "@rules_cc//cc/toolchains/actions:source_compile_actions",
     ],
     args = [
         "-Xclang",
